    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
    "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
    "description": "This image shows the internal components of a Lenovo ThinkPad X220 with the black keyboard support bezel installed. The motherboard, FRU 04W3286, features a soldered Intel i5-2520M processor cooled by a Toshiba fan assembly, FRU 04W0435. A Crucial 2.5-inch Solid State Drive is installed in the main SATA bay. The full-size Mini PCIe slot is occupied by an Ericsson F5521gw module, a 3G mobile broadband card with built-in GPS that supports HSPA+ with download speeds up to 21 Mbps. The half-size Mini PCIe slot contains an AzureWave AW-AB116H, a dual-band Wi-Fi card based on the Atheros AR9462 chipset, supporting 802.11n up to 300 Mbps and Bluetooth 4.0. Additionally, a separate Bluetooth module, FRU 60Y3271, is installed. This is a Broadcom BCM92070MD card providing Bluetooth 3.0 connectivity",
    "width": 1600,
    "height": 996
  },
